; t24_refsem.n — reference semantics: a container handle IS the object.
; Mutation ops (append/pop/set/…) act in place; every name bound to the same
; handle sees the change, and growth never re-allocates the handle — no
; re-store after append.
; Expected: stdout "ok\n"; rc 0.
entry:
list a!
a b!                          ; alias: both names denote the same list
40 grow for                  ; grow far past the initial capacity
a length 40 eq check          ; original name sees every append
b length 40 eq check          ; alias sees them too — b was never re-stored
b 7 get 7 eq check            ; values readable through the alias
b pop consume                 ; pop mutates in place
a length 39 eq check          ; …visible through the other name
dict d!
d e!
100 dfill for                ; crosses the dict's growth threshold
d length 100 eq check
e length 100 eq check
e 50 get 50 eq check
"ok" print
ret
grow: k! a k append consume ret
dfill: k! d k k set ret
